<title>USA: Thomas &amp; Betts chief details Augat purchase.</title>
<headline>Thomas &amp; Betts chief details Augat purchase.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomas &amp; Betts Corp chairman Kevin Dunnigan said his company's $559 million purchase of Augat Inc would yield roughly between $0.03 to $0.05 a share in 1997 and more than $0.10 a share in 1998 to profits.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to become accretive in the second half of 1997, Dunnigan told analysts on a conference call on Monday shortly after Thomas &amp; Betts announced its agreement to buy Augat.</p>
</text>
